From d7079265ea1263a1af6cd9cd132fc18dcb1793d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bradley Gleave <bradley@bradleytgpcoaching.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:24:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: make react-native-mmkv a bundle-safe optional
 dependency

`expo export --platform android` failed on main and on the S6 candidate with
"Unable to resolve module react-native-mmkv from src/storage/mmkv.ts" even
though the package is intentionally undeclared and the AsyncStorage shim is
the intended persistence layer.

Root cause: Metro (with Expo's allowOptionalDependencies) only tolerates an
unresolvable specifier while every require() of it sits directly inside a
try block. src/storage/mmkv.ts required the package twice: a guarded probe
and an unguarded require inside the MmkvStorage constructor. The second one
demoted the dependency to required; Metro reported the first location, so
the try/catch looked sufficient when it was not.

Fix (narrow, no dependency/native/flag changes):
- require the module exactly once, directly inside a try block, and hand the
  loaded module to MmkvStorage instead of re-requiring it;
- decide availability from the loaded module's shape (asMmkvModule: must
  expose an MMKV constructor) rather than from "require did not throw";
- export isMmkvAvailable() for truthful capability reporting.

Namespaces (prefs:/cache:/secure:), the AsyncStorage shim, clearAllStorage
(sign-out wipe) and the MMKV path's configuration are behaviourally unchanged;
the MMKV path stays inactive because the package remains absent.

Tests:
- declaredDependencies guard: replace the stale claim that try/catch alone
  protects Metro; parse shipped source and assert the package is required
  from exactly one Metro-optional site, has no static import/re-export/
  dynamic import, and remains absent from package.json and the lockfile.
- new src/storage/__tests__/mmkv.test.ts: shape detection, shim fallback,
  namespace layout/isolation, logout wipe leaves foreign keys.
